content.text:
Mobile title at 844x390: content extends beyond bottom (credits cut off). Title menu uses absolute or grid; at 390 height, 5 buttons don't fit. Need fix responsive layout for short landscape. The screenshot shows bottom cut at "CRÉDITOS". The title screen probably uses 100vh with padding; but menu starts y=185 and buttons 44px each + gaps = 250, ending at 435 > 390. Need compact vertical layout at max-height 500: reduce title heading and button heights, gap, maybe hide feature cards, move menu. Also title side cards not visible in mobile because likely hidden by media query? Fine.

Mobile game: touch controls are not visible! Settings touch auto should show because pointer coarse? Playwright desktop browser has maxTouchPoints 0 and pointer fine, so auto hides. To test touch we can force setting touch 'on'. Do that and screenshot. Also HUD: top-left character badge overlaps? At mobile, name and bars okay. The quest tracker and creature chip are hidden by `hud-side { display:none }` at max-height 500. Good. Toasts on right side overlap but okay.

Need fix mobile title. Also title at 844 width: left aligned, sword center; menu only left half. Could be okay. But bottom cut. We'll add CSS @media (max-height: 500px) rules:
```
.title-screen { padding: 10px 16px; justify-content: flex-start? }
.game-title span { font-size: 34px }
.title-menu { gap:4px; margin-top:4px }
.title-menu .btn { min-height:32px; padding:5px 12px; font-size:9.5px }
.title-sub { margin: 2px 0 6px; }
.title-kicker maybe smaller.
.title-emblem { width:32;height:32 }
```
Need inspect title CSS structure to know.

